test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T16:27:59.3111489Z             "body": "This draft preserves the original local stdio MCP and adds bounded batch/jobs, private profiles/artifacts, production packaging, lifecycle checks and native evidence. Release acceptance remains blocked.\n\nValid journal reopens now avoid resetting an unchanged SQLite schema version. The old assignment adds a4,120-byte WAL frame; real Node22/24 observations and38 journal/controller regressions per Node verify the conditional assignment preserves exact WAL bytes, durable state and integrity. Fresh schema/version creation remains in the original transaction, with FULL sync, identity/schema validation, checkpoint, busy and RPC limits unchanged. A controlled real SQLite write reproduces the old frame and fails the new regression. This is not a cause-fix claim for the Windows progress timeout.\n\nThe pinned VP9 encoder declares BT.709 primaries alongside its smpte170m matrix. Actual Mac WebKit recording passes the unchanged decoded-red threshold in native88 and89. Prepared core SHA256: 3eb68a089871529d6dccd723546bc87e20299047e140d382dc5fe380b1350192. Windows WebKit PCM/VP9 readiness remains a strict failure despite valid ranges.\n\nFailed journal fixtures preserve stores and propagate close failures; controlled negatives confirm real worker exits before injected errors. Bounded CI checkpoints expose only test-receipt numbers (every25, cap16), with no payload/pass/cleanup claims. Docker context is restricted to16 existing inputs, validated by a scratch export and native image build/hash checks. Linux batch setup uses the canonical HTTPS Ubuntu archive after measured Azure fetch stalls, preserving apt signatures/package requirements and the30m budget.\n\nNative89 at8416021: completed summaries1967 passes/6 failures. All Linux batch lanes and all four component lanes pass; all five installed-package steps succeed (Mac from REST metadata only). Original582/2: Linux192/0, Mac192/0, Windows190/2, plus Docker2/0, legacy3/0 and fresh Mac modal3/0. All12 independent traces and12 PDF behaviors pass. Mac main batch was cancelled at30m and its log remained empty on two reads; outcomes/cleanup are unobserved. Actual Windows client recovered CRASHED with750 recorded actions, no result and operator attention required after rpc_timeout/progress; worker/browser cleanup is unconfirmed. Actual Mac943 times out. Historical136/142 PID counts, native87 scoped observation and other unknown exits remain retained without filtering or debt clearance.\n\nLocal candidate validation: fresh297-file scripts-disabled production installation and real original/profile/batch/jobs/controller/journal/guardian checks pass. Strict TypeScript, README generation, bounded checkpoint parsing/replays and artifact checks pass. Actionlint was run with shellcheck/pyflakes disabled. No existing assertion, action/RPC/test/job limit, browser/transport default or unsafe-replay rule is weakened.\n\nNative90 source58edfce:\n- [Local batch QA](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39803246586)\n- [Original CI](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39803246848)\n\nExact scope and gaps: docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT.md, docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md, docs/evidence/native89-summary.json. No merge or publishing is requested while critical gates remain open.\n",
